## Session summary

**Criteria ("all known issues resolved") — NOT met yet; substantial progress made.** The pve physical nodes were down (no OOB), so I pivoted to the VM rig (test1/test2 + rebuilt LIO tcm_loop shared LUN), where the handoff's dialloc-corruption family reproduces in 45–180s of 2-node churn — every round, with full dmesg autopsies.

**Six fixes landed (v0.11.40 → 0.11.46, all uncommitted per standing rules):**
1. **Dead-shell CREATE fix** (the exact pve signature): defer the false "Corruption detected!" check for peer-freed IRECLAIMABLE shells + sanitize them from disk evidence in recycle. **Verified rescuing live** — the previously-fatal chain now completes the create (fired on both nodes, zero resulting corruption).
2. **Recycle-gate ordering guard** — stop adopting older-generation disk images (proven mis-adopt on ino 1862).
3. **P116 zombie arm** — a clean gen+1 disk-free image is a peer-freed zombie: adopt it so stale-map truncates no-op (kills the double extent-free feeder).
4. **Own-free bypass** — an unpublished reused create's rightful freer no longer misclassifies its own life as peer-freed (this was leaking AGI bucket entries and inobt allocations; proven via ino 680).
5. **AGI bucket unleak + intent-flag/generation hygiene** at every reuse point.
6. **Busy-extent duplicate guard** — upstream's duplicate-insert path infinite-loops holding a spinlock (proven 2-CPU wedge that starved the peer's DLM into a 184s-timeout shutdown); now logs and bails.

**Result:** first-ever clean churn rounds (2 consecutive) on v0.11.45. The one remaining corruption flavor is now precisely instrumented: P150 record-level traces prove the two nodes hold **divergent inobt record copies across AG handoffs** (restamp/keep-in-core family; cold re-reads nearly absent — bgen=0, ~1 read per 14 writes). The next session has a ranked root-candidate list and a one-shot discriminator (P144 WR/RD cross-node join) recorded in memory (`ccloop4dd7-sess1-C-inobt-divergence-root-lead`), plus open items: DLM timeout-escalation policy, dead-peer journal recovery, AGI Phase-B, pve2 flush_workqueue wedge, and final multi-round + full-suite verification.

